    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8cc0806f_ba2ac392",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnCommandBuffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 456,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-10T20:03:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is so similar to the data being sent as the render area. Do you have any plans to consolidate these extensions?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 440,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 456,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "fca71b3eca817d1b5183ac324e2d6189fea9b0b5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9df1d281_879ad7a5",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnCommandBuffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 456,
      "author": {
        "id": 14669
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-10T20:33:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can\u0027t 100% consolidate them because the partial resolve bounds do two things. They put a bounding rect on the resolve area which RenderPassRenderArea can do. They also allow using a MSAA texture that doesn\u0027t match resolve texture size. We could add support for RenderPassRenderArea in D3D11 Dawn backend and then pass less info in this struct?  I\u0027d have to discuss with @lehoangquyen@chromium.org in more detail.",
      "parentUuid": "8cc0806f_ba2ac392",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 440,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 456,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "fca71b3eca817d1b5183ac324e2d6189fea9b0b5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ccfd9a96_4671fdff",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnCommandBuffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 456,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-11T13:24:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, I suppose it would mean we\u0027d be using the RenderPassRenderArea in addition to the rest of the PartialLoadResolve struct that specifies the color offset. That does feel a little awkward to have to remember to use both extensions together.",
      "parentUuid": "9df1d281_879ad7a5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 440,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 456,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "fca71b3eca817d1b5183ac324e2d6189fea9b0b5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e6be4eb8_4b9a7371",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/mtl/MtlCommandBuffer.mm",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 607,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-10T20:03:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should either keep using `fRenderTargetBounds` here or update the `Intersects` check on line 358 to use `fRenderAreaBounds` for consistency.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 607,
        "startChar": 55,
        "endLine": 607,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "fca71b3eca817d1b5183ac324e2d6189fea9b0b5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8b4d6203_88e94484",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/mtl/MtlCommandBuffer.mm",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 607,
      "author": {
        "id": 14669
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-10T20:33:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ll leave it using fRenderTargetBounds to avoid unnecessary changes in this CL. I could also leave the Vulkan backend using fRenderTargetBounds if you like?",
      "parentUuid": "e6be4eb8_4b9a7371",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 607,
        "startChar": 55,
        "endLine": 607,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "fca71b3eca817d1b5183ac324e2d6189fea9b0b5",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a6c99460_4ecce70c",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/mtl/MtlCommandBuffer.mm",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 607,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-11T13:24:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think updating the Vulkan backend to use fRenderAreaBounds is more correct, it certainly helps to guard against higher-level bounds checks ever accidentally getting something wrong that would lead to a render area violation due to some bad math in a vertex shader, etc. Since metal doesn\u0027t have that, there\u0027s no real risk there so leaving it as render target bounds is fine.",
      "parentUuid": "8b4d6203_88e94484",
